<DIV dir=3Dltr id=3Dmw-content-text lang=3Den class=3Dmw-content-ltr>
<H2><SPAN id=3DSummary class=3Dmw-headline>Summary</SPAN></H2>
<P>The touch gauge is the crescent bar on the bottom corners of the =
screen. When=20
the bar is full, you can use "touch" whenever you want by pressing the =
touch=20
button during different situations. After using touch, it only takes a =
couple of=20
seconds before it completely recharges and you can use touch again. =
There are 5=20
different types of touch techniques that you can use during a fight. =
</P>
<H2><SPAN id=3DTouch_Types class=3Dmw-headline>Touch Types</SPAN></H2>
<P><B><FONT size=3D3>Normal Touch </FONT></B></P>
<P><A class=3Dimage =
href=3D"http://wiki.mizuumi.net/w/File:Normaltouch.png"><IMG=20
alt=3DNormaltouch.png =
src=3D"http://wiki.mizuumi.net/images/0/0a/Normaltouch.png"=20
width=3D1375 height=3D250></A> </P>
<P>A normal touch is performed at neutral. </P>
<P>This version has a long period of recovery, but your partner will =
receive the=20
ability of the exiting character for a short period of time. This can be =
very=20
useful when you have a free moment. It takes roughly 3 seconds for the =
touch=20
gauge to refill after a normal touch, and it removes roughly 50% of the =
current=20
break limit. </P>
<P>Upon normal touch, all "flashing" health will be restored instantly, =
similar=20
to red health in Capcom tag fighters. </P>
<P><BR><B><FONT size=3D3>Attack Touch </FONT></B></P>
<P><A class=3Dimage =
href=3D"http://wiki.mizuumi.net/w/File:Attack_touch.png"><IMG=20
alt=3D"Attack touch.png"=20
src=3D"http://wiki.mizuumi.net/images/a/a7/Attack_touch.png" =
width=3D1375=20
height=3D250></A> </P>
<P>An attack touch is performed when you are in the middle of an attack. =
</P>
<P>Attack touch can be used to created longer and more damaging combos =
with both=20
of your characters. Also, the attack that your partner does when =
entering the=20
stage is an overhead attack. So you can also use this while your =
opponent is=20
defending for a surprise attack. It takes roughly 6 seconds for the =
touch gauge=20
to refill after an attack touch, and it removes roughly 25% of the =
current break=20
limit. </P>
<P>Attack touching applies a flat rate to your combo scaling, reducing =
damage to=20
roughly 80%. </P>
<P><BR><B><FONT size=3D3>Guard Touch </FONT></B></P>
<P><A class=3Dimage =
href=3D"http://wiki.mizuumi.net/w/File:Guard_touch.png"><IMG=20
alt=3D"Guard touch.png" =
src=3D"http://wiki.mizuumi.net/images/0/0d/Guard_touch.png"=20
width=3D1386 height=3D252></A> </P>
<P>Guard touches are done while your current character is blocking. It =
requires=20
1 bar from your partner's SP gauge. </P>
<P>A Guard Touch will cause your opponent to stagger while you switch =
places=20
with your partner. Letting yourself become guard broken is very =
dangerous, so=20
you can make use of these to stop your opponents rushdown and =
reestablish=20
neutral ground. It takes roughly 9 seconds for the touch gauge to refill =
after a=20
guard touch, and it removes roughly 50% of the current break limit. </P>
<P>In patch x.xx, Guard touch was split to be two different =
touches--Normal=20
guard touch and Knock-back Guard Touch. To perform the stronger =
knock-back=20
version of Guard touch, block an attack, press forward while blocking =
and press=20
the touch button. If done successfully, the opponent will flash red as =
they are=20
knocked back. Attacking the opponent during the stun frames of the =
stronger=20
knock-back applies a flat rate to your damage scaling, reducing damage =
to=20
roughly 70%. </P>
<P><BR></P>
<P><B><FONT size=3D3>Damage Touch </FONT></B></P>
<P><A class=3Dimage =
href=3D"http://wiki.mizuumi.net/w/File:Damage_touch.png"><IMG=20
alt=3D"Damage touch.png"=20
src=3D"http://wiki.mizuumi.net/images/6/66/Damage_touch.png" =
width=3D1386=20
height=3D252></A> </P>
<P>You can use damage touch while you're receiving damage. This costs 2 =
bars=20
from your partner's SP gauge. </P>
<P>Damage touch will blow your opponent away from your with a burst like =

animation, then switch your partner in. This could come in handy when =
you feel=20
that you might be stunned soon. Note that this will not work against =
projectile=20
attacks. It takes roughly 15 seconds for the touch gauge to refill after =
a=20
damage touch, and it removes roughly 50% of the current break limit. =
</P>
<P><BR><B><FONT size=3D3>Assault Touch </FONT></B></P>
<P><A class=3Dimage =
href=3D"http://wiki.mizuumi.net/w/File:Assult_touch.png"><IMG=20
alt=3D"Assult touch.png"=20
src=3D"http://wiki.mizuumi.net/images/a/ad/Assult_touch.png" =
width=3D1386=20
height=3D252></A> </P>
<P>Assault touch is performed with <B>236D</B> and requires 2 bars from =
your=20
partner's SP gauge. </P>
<P>Assault touch will cause your character to perform a full screen rush =
towards=20
the opponent; you will have full body invincibility during this time. On =
hit,=20
you will blow your opponent away and then switch with your partner. You =
can do=20
this to punish almost any technique from a distance and force a close =
range=20
battle. It takes roughly 15 seconds for the touch gauge to refill after =
an=20
assault touch, and it removes roughly 50% of the current break limit. =
</P>
<P>In later versions, the entering character will receive the ability of =
the=20
exiting character for a short period of time. </P>
<P><BR></P>
